<section xml:id="exercises">
    <title>Exercises</title>
      <exercise>
        <statement>
          <p>
            Let <m>G = (N,E)</m> be a weighted graph with distinguished vertices <m>s</m> and <m>t</m> and edge
            <m>(t,s)</m>. Let <m>\vec{c} \in \mathbb{R}^{E}</m>. Define the weighted cost of a circulation as
            <me>\vec{c} \cdot \vec{w} = \sum_{(u,v) \in E} c_{(u,v)}w_{(u,v)}</me>.
            Suppose that <m>\vec{c}</m> is non-negative and <m>c_{(t,s)} =0</m>. Then the minimum cost of a non-negative weighted circulation <m>\vec{w}</m> such that <m>\vec{w}_{(s,t)} \neq 0</m> is the
            minimum length of a weighted shortest path with edge weights <m>\vec{c}</m>.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </exercise>
    </section>